/* state: held | swept | broken | untested   (status colour + icon + label, never colour alone) */
/* ============================ MHI, ON THE FUTURE ============================
   Every level on the Hong Kong board used to be measured on the CASH Hang Seng
   index — what the relay carries — while every fill happens on the Mini-Hang Seng
   future. The card said so and then carried a basis to convert between them, and
   a basis is not a constant: this page's own measurement had it running +29, -5,
   +22, +15, +16 across a single week, thirty-five points of wander at HK$10 a
   point, which is worse than the feed error it was correcting.

   This block is the fix, and the fix is not a better basis — it is not needing
   one. 1,382 fifteen-minute bars from HKFE, 10 July to 10 August, 723,458
   contracts of real transacted volume, which is the one thing a cash index cannot
   provide at any price because an index has no volume at all. The profile, the
   point of control, the value area, the typical thirty-minute travel and the turn
   counts below are all measured on the contract that gets traded.

   WHAT IT IS NOT: a live feed. It is regenerated by hand from a broker pull, so
   every figure carries `pulled` and goes stale after it — the card prints that
   date rather than letting a reader assume otherwise. And the bars are fifteen
   minutes where ES and RTY get five, so every count here is a coarser observation
   than its equivalent on those boards. Both are said out loud on the card.

   THE BASIS IS NOW REFUSED RATHER THAN QUOTED, and that is a finding rather than
   a retreat. Across 61 instants where both series print, the middle half of the
   measurements spans 23.7 points against a 22.8-point floor set by the cash
   feed's OWN bar-to-bar movement — so what looked like a basis is dominated by
   the two feeds not being stamped at the same moment. Tightening the match from
   300 seconds to 30 was tried first and changed nothing (61 samples became 60,
   the distribution was identical), which rules out timestamp slop and leaves feed
   lag. The -5.8 this board used to publish was false precision by an order of
   magnitude. Generated by mhigen.py. */
