/* THE MEASUREMENT DATE OF A BAKED BLOCK, in the voice the scenario branches use
   for "as built". One function rather than one per painter, for the reason the
   house rules give for deriving a list: three cards carry this today, a fourth
   the next time a generator learns to declare a missing input, and three
   hand-written copies is three places for the wording and the logic to drift.

   WHY EVERY BAKED CARD, not only a carried-forward one. These blocks never move
   between bakes -- they are computed against the archive at refresh time -- so
   their age is worth stating on any build. The carried-forward NOTE is the extra
   sentence, added only when REFRESH_SKIPS names the block, because that is the
   case where the date is older than the page around it.

   `gen` travels inside the block, written by the generator that made it, so this
   is measured rather than remembered: it cannot drift away from the numbers
   beside it without the numbers moving too.

   ON window, and formatting its own date, because the three painters that call
   it live in three different scopes on this page and none of them is the global
   one. Borrowing smtUTC from the agreement card's scope threw for the other two. */
window.genStamp = function(name, blk, nowMs){
  var gen = blk && blk.gen;
  if (!gen) return '';
  var carried = !!(typeof REFRESH_SKIPS !== "undefined" && REFRESH_SKIPS && REFRESH_SKIPS[name]);
