/* Time at price for NQ, ES and RTY. Generated by tapgen.py on every refresh;
   never edited by hand.

   THIS IS NOT A VOLUME PROFILE AND THE BLOCK CARRIES ITS OWN PROXY ERROR.
   The relay banks five-minute bars for ES and RTY only, so NQ has no volume at
   any price and never will. What is measured instead is how long the quote
   stood in each price bin, with two corrections that are forced by the feed
   rather than chosen: intervals where the quote did not change are dropped (a
   clock-sampled feed otherwise banks an entire closed weekend into one bin --
   28% of ES's time against 0.7% of its volume), and any interval longer than
   CAP seconds is truncated, so a publisher outage cannot read as conviction at
   the last price before it. `cal` is the whole comparison against real volume
   on ES, and the painter prints it.

   `air.x` IS A TESTED CLAIM AND IT FAILS ON NQ. It is the median six-minute
   step inside the voids over the median inside the shelves -- the "price moves
   fast through thin prices" belief, measured. ES 3.33x, RTY 1.22x, NQ 0.96x.
   `swp` re-measures it at six bin widths with the void sample size carried,
   because a ratio that only survives one cut of the bins is a result about the
   cut. Any painter that shows a void must read air.x for THAT symbol before
   describing it as fast.

   `tl` IS THE RANGE THE MODEL DOES NOT CLASSIFY -- below the lowest shelf
   and above the highest. It exists because a painter that draws only shelves
   and voids leaves that range blank, and blank reads as "nothing happened"
   when on a trending contract it means "this is where the contract started
   and it has not been back". Carries `last`, seconds since price was inside.

   `hsi` IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A PROFILE, AND THE HEADLINE REPEAT RATE IS A
   TRAP. `held` is taken over the whole archive, 85% of which is hours the
   Hong Kong exchange is shut; across those hours the quote repeats 99% of
   the time because there is nothing for it to do. In the weekday cash
   session it repeats 14%, and with the 12:00-13:00 HKT lunch halt removed,
   5%. `sheld`/`lheld`/`oheld` carry the split so no painter can quote the
   archive figure alone. The board is refused for sample size and for the
   total absence of volume, NOT because the feed is dead -- it is not. */
